module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.record_value_escapes_declared_optional_return

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { CurrentRungUnstatedAfterClimb, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

data record_value_escapes_declared_optional_return: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "record_value_escapes_declared_optional_return" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: CurrentRungUnstatedAfterClimb },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: in the v1 seed, two independent non-rejections let a wrong-typed value stand where a declared type is required, with ZERO blocking diagnostics. (A) `Present { value: <record R> }` returned from a fn declared `-> T?` where T is a coproduct. (B) a bare record R returned from a fn declared `-> T` where T is a coproduct. Each is accepted; the one-axis green (`Present { value: r.arch }`, `r.arch`) is accepted too. The cross-type `==` seen in the same specimen is a different class, filed as a receipt on cross_type_comparison_answers_instead_of_refusing, so the acceptance is a missing judgment and not a blanket. A bare record at `T?` IS refused (declared Optional<Arch>, produced Row), which locates (A) at the Optional wrapper.",

    "SPECIMEN (snappy-seal-211, gunbc#14063 before 20d205c7529, in-tree RED at e5d277c5c42): extdeps.cpu.types soc_family_architecture was declared `-> Architecture?`, took `lead`, the first CpuModelCatalogRow of the family, compared `m.architecture == lead` (field against row: always false) and returned `Present { value: lead }` (a row where an Architecture was declared). v2-bootstrap was green. HARM: every SoC family established no architecture, which silently emptied the reset roster. A SILENT WRONG ANSWER, DESIGN section 5, outside the ladder. It was found by a reviewer reading the fold, not by any gate.",

    "THE CHAIN, DESIGN section 6b. The two declared-type judgments are split. `declared_type_conformance_diags_core` (src/v1/04_infer.dag), the one the declared-return and data-initializer positions consult, has no arm for a product at a declared coproduct, so (B) falls through; `product_versus_coproduct_head_mismatch` exists but is reached only from `declared_type_inhabitance`. That judgment answers UndecidableOptionalCarrier whenever EITHER side is optional, and never compares the Optional payloads, so (A) abstains exactly where the payload is the whole question. Earliest unjustified boundary: the declared-type obligation abstaining on the Optional payload and on the product-versus-coproduct head, not the fn that returned the row.",

    "SAME CLASS AS THE BallGridArray PROBE (extdeps.cpu.types, comment on SocketTermination)? SAME FAMILY, DIFFERENT HOLE. Both are the checker resolving or accepting a value without testing it against the declared coproduct it must inhabit, and both were found in extdeps.cpu.types. BallGridArray is a bare VARIANT NAME resolved from the pool and never tested for membership in the declared coproduct (a wrong arm of the right type, stored or compared, never matched). This one is a whole RECORD VALUE of the wrong type escaping a declared Optional or coproduct return, . Distinguishing fact: the BGA probe is silent only while the value is stored or compared, a total `match` is a runtime guard; here the value reaches the caller as a Present of the wrong type and the wrong `==` never matches anything, so no later match refuses it. Related rows, not duplicates: bare_value_admitted_where_optional_is_declared (cardinality only), generic_coproduct_argument_unjudged_at_declared_return (applied argument, not Optional payload), cross_type_comparison_answers_instead_of_refusing (record vs scalar literal: refused for coproducts, answers for records), a_record_accepted_where_a_declared_scalar_slot_is_declared (scalar slot, not coproduct or Optional).",

    "NATIVE v2: NOT MEASURED HERE. I did not measure (A) or (B) on a native v2 build (the cross-type `==` is recorded under comparison_operands_never_judged_in_v2_infer). v2.std.inhabitance declared_type_inhabitance is the v2 counterpart of the seed's judgment; whether it descends the Optional payload is the open question. Do not read this row as saying v2 is clean.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: below the floor (silently admitted), DESIGN section 4b: values inhabit declared types. CEILING: structurally guaranteed, decidable from the declared type and the produced type at the site. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY: the declared-type obligation descends the Optional layer to judge the payload, and refuses a product at a declared coproduct at every position that consults it, original trigger, satisfied by gunbc#14178: sufficient that the two enrolled reds (A, B) in `test.claim.record_escapes_declared_optional_return_witness` turn green while the two controls stay green. gunbc#14178 climbed A and B. gunbc#14185 added C and C-prime and retired the expected-red chunk `floor_expected_red_chunk_record_escapes_declared_optional_return` from `v2.workflow.floor_expected_red`. `w_a_record_at_a_declared_coproduct_return_is_refused` and `w_a_record_inside_present_at_a_declared_optional_coproduct_is_refused` in `test.claim.record_escapes_declared_optional_return_witness` stay enrolled as permanent regression controls (DESIGN section 4b, meta-obligation 4).",

    "CLIMBED FOR A AND B (gunbc#14178, calm-crane-178, declared-type fix): `declared_type_conformance_diags_core` now has a product-versus-coproduct arm reusing `product_versus_coproduct_head_mismatch`, and `present_payload_declared_from_optional` hands the peeled declared payload of a plain `T?` to every `Present { value: .. }` payload whatever its syntax. Executed on a runner at this tree: `w_a_record_inside_present_at_a_declared_optional_coproduct_is_refused` and `w_a_record_at_a_declared_coproduct_return_is_refused` PASS, their one-axis-green and liveness controls PASS, and a second required-regen round exits 0. The boundary is product-versus-coproduct judgment of a Present payload at a plain `T?` only, not general recursive Optional conformance: an alias or a nominal `Optional<T>` expected abstains (the nominal arm of the new helper was removed after review; no red or green pair covers the nominal form, so it stays open), and native v2 is still unmeasured. The two claims left the expected-red roster and stay as permanent regression controls (DESIGN 4b(4)). gunbc#14185 adds the climb for C and C-prime (cross-type `==`/`!=`): `equality_admission_diags` calls `equality_operands_never_inhabit_together`, and the expected-red chunk is retired; all four regression claims (A, B, C, C-prime) stay enrolled as permanent controls. The whole-corpus covering compile named by declared_type_wall_keyed_on_the_value_being_a_kernel did not run as a differential: closure load and normalize now pass (#14183) but it then OOMs at 24 GiB and BuildBuddy refuses it, so the new-refusal population is bounded by an entry differential and judged by the CI floor, not by that instrument. The differential ran each of 60 entries as `gunbc run --function __no_such_function__` on main, on this tree and on the == operand tree: 57 of 60 completed on all three with 0 blocking diagnostics, and none of the completed entries showed an A-only or B-only refusal. Three are unresolved: fleet/site_pxe_edge_converge and instruments/tier_o_drift_check exceeded the 900s cap on all three sides (not attributable to these changes), and roadmap/roadmap_launch_deployment_cli was killed (exit 137) on main only under parallel load while both trees completed it. The probe sees only entries that already refuse at rc=1, so it bounds new flags and does not prove none.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
